§ `C. Reg 3: deemed foreign residents`

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      days  IS A `Days in Israel`
      imm   IS A BOOLEAN
      five  IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      cl    IS A `A class in regulation 3`
      arr   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`a person in` y `with` days `, new immigrant:` imm `, foreign in the five years before:` five `, class` cl `, arrived` arr MEANS
    `the individual in` y `with` days `, found` NOTHING `, ties` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE `, regulation 2` NOTHING
        `, regulation 3` (JUST (`Facts for regulation 3` WITH
                                   `a new immigrant within section 35(d)` IS imm,
                                   `a foreign resident in each of the five preceding tax years, oldest first` IS five,
                                   `the class` IS cl,
                                   `the day he arrived in Israel` IS arr))
        `, section 14(b)` NOTHING

`five foreign years` MEANS LIST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`the 200 days` MEANS `days counted` 200 `,` 0 `,` 0
`a diplomat` MEANS `a diplomatic representative or consular official of a foreign state in regular service and official capacity, or a spouse or child living with one`
`a foreign soldier` MEANS `a soldier of a foreign army or in the service of the United Nations`
`a teacher` MEANS `a teacher, lecturer or researcher serving a higher-education or other teaching institution`
`a cleric` MEANS `a member of the clergy filling a religious post in an institution in Israel at its invitation`
`a journalist or athlete` MEANS `a foreign journalist or a foreign athlete as described in section 75A`
`no class` MEANS `none of these classes`

GIVEN asked IS A BOOLEAN
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A class in regulation 3`
`an IDF newcomer, who asked:` asked `, service ended` ended MEANS `one who came to Israel to serve in the Israel Defense Forces, until the end of his military service` WITH `the day his military service ended` IS ended, `he asked not to be regarded as an Israeli resident` IS asked

GIVEN asked IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A class in regulation 3`
`a student, who asked:` asked MEANS `a student studying at least half of a programme` WITH `he asked not to be regarded as an Israeli resident` IS asked

GIVEN came IS A BOOLEAN
      h0 IS A NUMBER
      h1 IS A NUMBER
      h2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A class in regulation 3`
`a patient: ` came `, hospitalised` h0 `,` h1 `,` h2 MEANS `a hospital patient` WITH `he came to Israel for hospitalisation, or fell ill while in Israel` IS came, `the days of hospitalisation in the tax year` IS h0, `the days of hospitalisation in the tax year before it` IS h1, `the days of hospitalisation in the tax year before that` IS h2

GIVEN cl IS A `A class in regulation 3`
      y IS A NUMBER
      arr IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`resident with class` cl `in` y `, arrived` arr MEANS `independent resident` (`a person in` y `with` `the 200 days` `, new immigrant:` FALSE `, foreign in the five years before:` `five foreign years` `, class` cl `, arrived` arr) `under` `D`

